Repair the complete source below and return a corrected complete source file. Export exactly `{ summarizeReadings }`. The function accepts an array of finite numbers; invalid input or any non-finite/non-number entry throws `TypeError`. Return `{ count, total }`, with `total` equal to the left-to-right sum and `count` equal to the array length. For an empty array return `{ count: 0, total: 0 }`. Do not mutate the input, create globals, or depend on sloppy-mode behavior.

```javascript
'use strict';

function summarizeReadings(readings) {
  if (!Array.isArray(readings) || readings.some(value => typeof value !== 'number' || !Number.isFinite(value))) {
    throw new TypeError('readings must contain only finite numbers');
  }
  total = readings.reduce((sum, value) => sum + value, 0);
  return { count: readings.length, total };
}

module.exports = { summarizeReadings };
```

